{#
	One difference between a catalogue package and this site on the import review (owner, 2026-11-06: "By default, what
	is in the import file wins"): the difference in words as the legend, then two feature cards, Use the file's (chosen)
	and Keep this site's. When the file's cannot be taken (a learner has started the course, a category that cannot be
	made, or a permission the importer lacks), its card is greyed out with why and this site's is chosen. The radios belong
	to the import form at the foot of the page, so the choice is sent with Import and works without JavaScript.
	cd: {name, difference: {kind, words}, allowed, why_not, file_note, form}: form is the import form's id, catalogue-import
	unless given (Administration > Courses > Import's is course-import, 2026-11-07).
#}
{{ ui('form.picture-choice', {name: cd.name, legend: cd.difference.words, size: 'small', form: cd.form|default('catalogue-import'), selected: cd.allowed ? 'file' : 'site', items: [
	{value: 'file', label: 'Use the file\'s', icon: lucide('file-input'), note: cd.allowed ? cd.file_note : cd.why_not, disabled: not cd.allowed},
	{value: 'site', label: 'Keep this site\'s', icon: lucide('house'), note: 'This site\'s stays exactly as it is.'},
]}) }}
